sub:assertion {
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/thompson1917-ch17-17> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/Claim>;
    dc:description "No continuous transformation series passes through known fossil and living human and anthropoid skulls (Mesopithecus, Pithecanthropus, Neanderthal, modern man), indicating that there is no single straight line of descent and that their variation has been divergent.";
    dc:type "historical-inference";
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Human and anthropoid skulls show divergent rather than linear evolutionary change";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/context> "D’Arcy Wentworth Thompson, On Growth and Form (1st ed., Cambridge: Cambridge University Press, 1917), Chapter XVII, “On the Theory of Transformations, or the Comparison of Related Forms”; topic “Human and ape skulls”. Scope: fossil and living hominids and anthropoid apes"
}
